\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Refinement ablations. ATE is unchanged in every row ($0.016975$ vs.\ a $0.0170$ baseline in the deterministic configuration): the map is strictly downstream of tracking, and the pre-registered failure condition ``ATE moves at all'' never fired. Freezing the Gaussian centres was separately measured optimal at both the online ($\sim $300-step) and offline (3000-step) budgets. The dedup row is included as a negative: it is a map-size control that costs quality when it fires without a recovery budget, not a quality feature.}}{10}{table.caption.32}\protected@file@percent }
